id: ops-i8yp
title: A release-completeness gate that requires every release tag to have a matching npm version and GitHub Release
description: "A release is a triple: a git tag, a published npm version, and a GitHub Release. When an earlier release step failed, tags and npm versions accumulated with no GitHub Release and nothing reported the gap. This gate audits the three lists for every release tag, requiring both a matching published npm version and a matching GitHub Release, and refuses orphan npm versions and orphan GitHub Releases whose corresponding tag is missing. The analysis is separated from the I/O so the rules are driven by injected lists, and tests are hermetic with no network."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-31T10:56:53.343Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-31T12:39:58.185Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-31T11:02:24.522Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-31T11:02:24.522Z"
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: "A release tag with no GitHub Release fails the gate; A release tag with no published npm version fails the gate; Orphan npm versions and orphan GitHub Releases fail the gate; The audit runs AFTER Create GitHub release and unconditionally, never from release:check, so it cannot block the step that would repair an incomplete predecessor"
value: "Detects the 14-day partial-release state that affected unbraind/pm-ops (v2026.08.28, v2026.08.29, v2026.08.31 published with no GitHub Release) and the same state in pm-context, pm-csv and pm-linear at v2026.08.09."
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-31T11:02:14.534Z",pi-agent,"Added scripts/verify-release-completeness.ts following verify-release-publish-attestation.ts conventions, with a hermetic suite of 25 tests driven by injected lists (no network). Wired into release:check via package.json. The 14-day partial-release evidence (v2026.08.28, v2026.08.29, v2026.08.31 published to npm with no GitHub Release while the newest GitHub Release was v2026.08.17) is encoded as a fixture. Reverting the audit logic to a no-op turns 6 defect-detecting tests red."
  "2026-08-31T12:39:58.185Z",claude-orchestrator,"Correction to two claims recorded earlier on this item, both flagged in review and both wrong. First, this gate is no longer wired into release:check. It was, and that was a P1 defect: release:check and prepublishOnly run before Create GitHub release, so an incomplete predecessor would have been rejected before the step that completes the current release could run, turning the exact fourteen-day outage this gate detects into an outage with no automated way out. The audit now runs as a workflow step after Create GitHub release, and unconditionally rather than only when should_release is true, because an incomplete predecessor is most likely to exist precisely on a day with nothing new to publish. Second, the recorded test list held 25 entries while the suite now has 31; the six added since have been recorded with their real test titles. Recorded rather than amended away, because an item whose stated contract no longer matches the code is the tracker equivalent of a green check over a gate that does not run."
